The tool of this package fetches the firmware of the NVIDIA graphics
adapters of this machine from download.nvidia.com and places it in
/boot/firmware/nvidia.  It checks the size and the hash of every file
against the pin table before it puts it in place.

The firmware is not in the package: a machine that has no network cannot
fetch it at the installation.  The firmware is fetched later with

	nvidia-firmware fetch

or taken from a directory of your own:

	nvidia-firmware fetch --from /path/to/the/files

nvidia-firmware status says what is in /boot/firmware/nvidia.

The nvidia module has to be unloaded before the tool can take a file away
from /boot/firmware/nvidia.
